| Question Type | Identification Clues | Approach / Strategy |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Path Identification** | Angle $\theta$ between $\vec{v}$ and $\vec{B}$. | $0/180^\circ \to$ Straight; $90^\circ \to$ Circle; Other $\to$ Helix. |
| **Comparison of Charges** | Protons, Alphas, Electrons in same $B$. | Use $R = \frac{mv}{qB}$ or $R \propto \frac{\sqrt{mK}}{q}$. Compare $m/q$ ratios. |
| **Combined Fields** | $\vec{E}$ and $\vec{B}$ given. | Check if forces balance ($v=E/B$). If not, use vector addition. |

| **Time Spent in Field** | Particle enters and exits at an angle. | $t = \frac{\theta_{arc}}{\omega} = \frac{m\theta_{rad}}{qB}$. |
