### **6. Common Mistakes and Traps**

| Mistake | Why Students Make It | Correct Approach |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Electron Direction** | Forgetting to flip the force for negative charges. | Perform $(\vec{v} \times \vec{B})$ and then **reverse** the direction for electrons. |
| **Speed Change** | Thinking magnetic fields can increase speed. | $\vec{B}$ can **never** change speed; only the Electric field ($\vec{E}$) can. |
| **Time Period Error** | Thinking a faster particle takes less time to orbit. | For a given $q, m, B$, the **time is constant** regardless of speed. |

